Casualty_Gender_Ratio\n# Feature description: Ratio of male casualties (Sex_of_Casualty = 1) to total casualties in an accident.\n# Usefulness: Incorporates the gender distribution of casualties, which might relate to driving behavior and patterns by the driver's gender.\ndf['Casualty_Gender_Ratio'] = df.groupby('Age_of_Driver')['Sex_of_Casualty'].transform(lambda x: (x == 1).sum() / len(x))\n```end\n\nStep 3: Classify Age into Risk Groups  \n```python\n# Feature name: Age_Risk_Group\n# Feature description: Classify Age_of_Driver into risk bands [low, medium, high] based on age brackets (e.g., <25, 25-65, >65).\n# Usefulness: Drivers in different age groups display distinct driving behaviors and accident profiles, which could correlate with their gender.\ndf['Age_Risk_Group'] = pd.cut(df['Age_of_Driver'], bins=[0, 25, 65, 100], labels=['low', 'medium', 'high'])\n```end\n\n---\n\n### Columns Dropped for Redundancy or Low Predictive Power  \n\nDrop `2nd_Road_Number`  \n```python\n# Explanation why the column 2nd_Road_Number is dropped\n# This column is sparse, with most values concentrated at 0.0, representing little variability or relevance to predicting the driver's sex.\ndf.drop(columns=['2nd_Road_Number'], inplace=True)\n```end  \n\nDrop `Vehicle_Location-Restricted_Lane`  \n```python\n# Explanation why the column Vehicle_Location-Restricted_Lane is dropped\n# The column contains mostly 0 values, indicating low signal and no strong correlation with the prediction of the driver's sex.\ndf.drop(columns=['Vehicle_Location-Restricted_Lane'], inplace=True)\n```end  \n\nDrop `Police_Force`  \n```python\n# Explanation why the column Police_Force is dropped\n# This column represents categorical values for different police forces, which likely correlate weakly with driver gender and provide no meaningful geographical or demographic insight beyond existing location features.\ndf.drop(columns=['Police_Force'], inplace=True)\n```end  "]
