Step 2: Compute Accident Density Factor  
python
# Feature name: Accident_Density_Factor
# Feature description: Multiply Urban_or_Rural_Area and Accident_Severity_Factor to account for accident density in different regions.
# Usefulness: Urban and rural areas may significantly differ in accident patterns and severity. This feature can highlight environment-based tendencies that may correlate with driver sex.
df['Accident_Density_Factor'] = df['Urban_or_Rural_Area'] * df['Accident_Severity_Factor']
end

Step 3: Ratio of Engine Capacity to Vehicle Age  
python
# Feature name: Engine_Capacity_to_Vehicle_Age_Ratio
# Feature description: Ratio of Engine_Capacity_(CC) to Age_of_Vehicle (adjusted to avoid division by 0).
# Usefulness: This captures how powerful a vehicle is compared to its age. Drivers with preferences for newer, high-capacity cars may reflect gender tendencies in vehicle choice, making this feature useful.
df['Engine_Capacity_to_Vehicle_Age_Ratio'] = df['Engine_Capacity_(CC)'] / (df['Age_of_Vehicle'] + 1)
end

